// Kev (CLASSIFICATION.md K4/K5): the gated delta rule, sequential over one
// segment's tokens, one workgroup a (v-head, segment).
//
// Per token, HF's torch_recurrent_gated_delta_rule for v-head h, which reads
// q/k head h / 2 (repeat_interleave: 32 v-heads over 16 k-heads, grouped):
//
//	S  <- S * exp(g)
//	d  <- (v - k^T S) * beta
//	S  <- S + k d^T
//	o  <- q^T S                     (q already carries 1/sqrt(128))
//
// with S [k=128][v=128]. Thread j owns column j of S in registers, so both
// dot products are a thread's own 128-long loop and the only sharing is q
// and k, staged through LDS once a token.
//
// **Segments.** Kev's row form runs each question from a copy of the state's
// cache; here the state is segment 0 and a branch reads the state's final S
